      "body": "## What\n`test_dsv41_bcg_hip.py` now asks the backend for the breakable graph's context width (`_graph_metadata_max_seq_len`) and checks the captured page table and the eager reference at that width, instead of assuming the capture batch's own width when no `max_seq_len` override is set.\n\n## Why\n`TestHipBreakableGraphCaptureReplay.test_capture_replay_matches_eager` has failed on every `stage-b-test-1-gpu-small-amd-mi35x` partition 0 run since Oct 19, on rocm10, rocm724 and rocm720:\n\n```\nFile \".../test_dsv41_bcg_hip.py\", line 168, in _capture_replay_matches_eager\n    self.assertEqual(\nAssertionError: 2 != 1\n```\n\nExample: https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39599109770/job/119218874753\n\nSince #43733, `_graph_metadata_max_seq_len` falls back to `prefill_cuda_graph_default_max_seq_len` (16k for the V4.1 1/2 layout) instead of `None` when `cuda_graph_config[prefill].max_seq_len` is unset. Capture therefore builds at 16k, and `page_table_from_req_to_token` caps that at the fixture's `req_to_token` width (512), giving 2 pages. The test still expected `ceil(96 / 256) = 1`. Replay rebuilds the live metadata at that same width, so the eager reference the test compares against has to be built at it too. The `max_context_size` branch of the test already did this; it now covers the default path.\n\nTest-only change.\n\n## Test plan\n- [ ] `stage-b-test-1-gpu-small-amd-mi35x`, all ROCm lanes, together with the other two fixes for this suite: https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39687298904\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39687371243](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39687371243)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39687370945](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39687370945)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39687370640](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39687370640)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
